+# EXL3 paired gate/up A-tile reuse: rejected
+
+Date: 2026-09-03
+
+## Verdict
+
+Reject the single-CTA paired gate/up experiment. It is bit-exact against the
+accepted M64 pipeline, but it is substantially slower at the expert row counts
+that dominate the synchronized long-prefill trace and is neutral to slightly
+slower at large row counts. The candidate was never wired into serving.
+
+## Candidate
+
+The accepted paired gate/up path launches one CTA for each 128-column tile of
+each matrix. The candidate halved the X grid by making one CTA compute the
+corresponding gate and up tiles together. It loaded each activation tile once,
+then loaded and decoded two packed-weight tiles and maintained two accumulator
+banks. The output order, EXL3 K4 MCG decode, FP32 accumulation, Hadamard
+scaling, SwiGLU and down/scatter stages were unchanged.
+
+- Source base: `7a7cfe2c9e`
+- Candidate image: `sparkglm-vllm:exl3-pairreuse-candidate-20260903a`
+- Head image ID: `c5be5ad6fa723085a0137111642d4b549dc59994032afa8a50755a43a7a13bc8`
+- Worker image ID: `b3d9c100886c1f5dd52aa550e6bd7f2cabf624ac0a8317de607fd3d845379be9`
+- Target: `sm_121a`, one GB10, CUDA events
+- Shape: hidden 4,096, TP-local intermediate 1,024, EXL3 K4 MCG
+- Timing: 20 warmups, 100 iterations, five alternating-order repeats; median
+- Timed pipeline: paired gate/up, fused SwiGLU/Hadamard and M64 down/scatter
+
+## Results
+
+Every tested row count produced bit-identical gate/up, post-SwiGLU/Hadamard and
+final down/scatter tensors (`max_abs=0`). Times are milliseconds per complete
+pipeline. Delta is candidate versus the accepted M64 pipeline; positive is
+slower.
+
