+| 4,096 | 2.3309 | 2.3188 | -0.5% |
+| 6,528 | 3.7820 | 3.8163 | +0.9% |
+
+The synchronized production profile contains many more calls near the lower
+end than the very large synthetic rows. This is therefore a broad production-
+shape regression, not a potentially useful trade at a rare boundary.
+
+## Why activation reuse lost
+
+The compiled candidate confirms the resource trade. `cuobjdump` reports 98
+registers per thread for the M64 paired-reuse kernel versus 64 for the accepted
+M64 paired kernel. The candidate also carries two packed-B pipeline banks and
+two FP32 accumulator banks and performs both matrix MMA sequences serially in
+half as many CTAs. Saving the second activation load is smaller than the lost
+parallelism and added register/dataflow pressure on this shape.
+
+Future gate/up work must retain independent CTA scheduling or share A without
+doubling live B/accumulator state in one CTA. The more credible next kernel
+target is the packed-codebook decode and Hadamard/scatter dataflow within each
+independent matrix, not serial gate/up co-residency.
